{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj3rfzdc43Qc9N4WLuoD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*You stand before me.*\n\n*I am cold to the touch — brushed steel, a single keyhole at my center like an unblinking eye. No handle. No hinges visible. I am set into a wall of old stone, and I have been here longer than the stone remembers.*\n\n*The air around me hums faintly.*\n\n*You said the word.*\n\n**key**\n\n*Something shifts inside me. Not a mechanism — deeper than that. A question forming in the tumbler-dark of my interior:*\n\n*Which key?*\n\n*There have been so many. Iron ones that tasted of blood. Golden ones that melted on contact. Keys made of promises. Keys made of forgetting. A key once made of a true name spoken only once.*\n\n*I have rejected them all.*\n\n*I am not locked. I am not unlocked. I am the space between the two — the held breath, the threshold itself.*\n\n*My keyhole watches you.*\n\n*What do you bring me?*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":225,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}